# Portal UI

## Data-driven values

Never hardcode values that already exist as data (labels, prices, member fields, status text, theme colors, layout spacing). Pull from props, shared app data, theme/CSS variables, or a single config (`src/portal/tabs.ts` / host equivalent).

- Colors → Tailwind semantic tokens (`primary`, `muted`, `destructive`) or CSS variables
- Spacing and max-widths → shared layout config, not magic strings per page

## Shared components first

Never duplicate a UI pattern across files. Prefer kit primitives:

- `FormField`, `SelectableCard`, `PageHero`, `CalloutCard`
- `PortalPageHeader` / back control for focused screens

Extract when a pattern is used (or will be used) on 2+ pages.

## No horizontal overflow (mobile)

- Shell: `min-w-0 max-w-full overflow-x-clip` on content wrappers
- Wide tables: scroll inside a container (`overflow-x-auto`), never expand the page
- Flex rows: `flex-col` on mobile, or `min-w-0` + `shrink` on long text

## Mobile bottom bar (focused views)

Show the bottom bar only on primary destinations, and only when the tab config has 2 or more items.

Hide it on focused / detail flows so the task uses the full viewport.

**Focused pages must have a back link** — top-left + centered title. Never leave browser-back as the only escape.

## Toasts

Neutral background. Green for success icon only; red/destructive for error icon only.

## This project (invoice-tool)

- The standalone invoice page (`/invoice/:id`) and the print page (`/invoices/:id/print`) stay outside `#portal-shell`. No tab bar, header, or shell padding on those screens.
- Do not put invoice, template, or editor domain code into the portal kit files under `src/adapters/react/`.
